  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This is naturally depending on the world, and the latency, but it is not uncommon that jumps are simply not registered. This might be because you have moved too far from geometry or that you have too high latency between vrc/headset/computer; But it presents a varying degree of annoyance, depending on the map-type. Naturally, the ones that are platforming-related is the worst affected, but this can be a nuissance even in more casual maps.\n\nI'd suggest implementing a grace-period from leaving geomtry, where pressing jump will still result in a jump being performed, similar to how many platformers have it. \n\nThis would be an overall quality-of-life improvement, while also enabling more creative map-types, that are more jump-dependent",
